[size=5][b]Nivalis Save Editor[/b][/size]
A small, standalone savegame editor for [b]Nivalis Nights[/b] by RenokK. Unofficial, not affiliated with ION LANDS.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Save browser[/b]: your saves with screenshots, location, in-game day and playtime, found automatically
[*][b]Money[/b]: set any amount, or add 1,000 / 10,000 / 100,000 credits with one click
[*][b]Inventory[/b]: edit your inventory, your venues' storage, fridges and furniture, and vendor stock. Add any of 1,300+ items by name, change quantities and freshness, or make all food fresh with one click
[*][b]Skills[/b]: set the level of your skills (Barter, Boat, Cooking, Farming, Fishing, Serving, Managing)
[*][b]People[/b]: edit friendship, romance, business and enemy levels for everyone you've met
[*][b]Venues[/b]: edit your venues' level and customers served, give all their reviews the same star rating, and see their seats, staff and storage
[*][b]Story variables[/b]: browse, search and edit 1,800+ game variables (relationships, venue levels, quest flags, …)
[*][b]Compare saves[/b]: see exactly what changed between two saves and copy values over
[*][b]Backups[/b]: up to 10 compressed backups per save, a comparison of what changed since each one, and one-click restore. The first backup of each save is kept permanently, and every edit is double-checked before it is written
[*][b]No restart needed[/b]: manual saves can be edited while the game is running. Save in the game, edit that save, load it again
[*][b]Safe by design[/b]: refuses to change the autosave while the game is running, warns you when a save comes from a game version it hasn't been tested with, and refuses to open saves it can't read correctly
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Download and extract the zip anywhere.
[*]Run [b]NivalisSaveEditor.exe[/b]. No installer, about 3 MB.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Usage[/b][/size]
Pick a save, change what you like, click [b]Save changes[/b], then load that save in the game.
Backups are stored outside the Steam Cloud save folder, in:
[code]%LOCALAPPDATA%\Nivalis Save Editor\Backups[/code]
Open the [b]Backups[/b] tab to compare or restore them.

[size=4][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The People and Venues screens are new in 1.2.0. If a change doesn't show up in the game as expected, please report it (and restore the backup).
[*]Story variables drive quests and dialogue. Changing them can skip or break quest steps, so experiment on a copy of a save first.
[*]The in-game clock and text variables are read-only for now.
[*]Steam Cloud syncs your saves, so an edited save replaces the cloud copy.
[*]The exe is not code-signed. If SmartScreen appears, click [i]More info → Run anyway[/i].
[*]Requires Windows 10/11 with WebView2 (built into Windows 11).
[/list]

[size=4][b]Planned[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Inspiration points
[*]Editing text variables
[/list]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
Tested with save format versions 151, 153 (the game patch of 1 October 2026) and 164 (the game update of October 2026). After a later game update the editor still opens your saves and warns you that the version is untested. If an update changes the save format so much that the editor can't read a save, it refuses to open it until it is updated.

[size=4][b]AI transparency[/b][/size]
This tool was built with the help of AI: [b]Claude Opus 5.5[/b] by Anthropic, used as a coding assistant. Claude did most of the reverse engineering of the save format and wrote most of the code, under my direction. I decided what the tool should do, tested it with my own saves in the game and approved each release. It also has an automated test suite that runs every edit against real save files.

The app itself contains no AI and doesn't connect to the internet. It only reads and writes your save files. The full source code is public on GitHub, so anyone can check what it does.

